 'task':'CARRIER-SOURCE-nontrivial-Kronecker-sum-factorization-no-go',
 'scientific_state':'PROVED_CURRENT_STRICT_12_CARRIER_DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_HIDDEN_NONTRIVIAL_CARTESIAN_PRODUCT_KRONECKER_SUM',
 'strict_offdiagonal_nonzero_ordered_entries':nonzero,
 'candidate_integer_factorizations_of_12':factorizations,
 'theorem':'For n,m>1, any matrix B tensor I_m + I_n tensor C has zero off-diagonal entries between product vertices (i,a) and (j,b) whenever i!=j and a!=b. A permutation cannot change the number of zero off-diagonal entries. The strict 12x12 Laplacian has nonzero coupling on every off-diagonal pair because every radial kernel weight d=1,...,6 is positive. Therefore it is not permutation-similar to any nontrivial Kronecker sum with 12=nm.',
 'consequence':'The d>1 product-carrier mechanism is a genuine new compositional extension, not a hidden factorization of the present strict 12-state operator.',
 'source_gap':'Current strict A therefore sources only its one cyclic/dihedral carrier. A theorem selecting additional independent carrier factors is still missing.',
